# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output
build/
dist/

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
.*.swp
**/*.DS_Store

# Generated by `npx grunt configTests` -- never commit these.
#
# They are derived entirely from src/core/operations/, so a committed copy goes stale the moment
# an operation changes, and an upstream sync then produces a diff nobody can review. Upstream
# gitignores exactly the same five paths; ours matched that list, except OperationConfig.json was
# ALSO tracked -- ignored and committed at once, because a `git add -f` in upstream-sync.yml put
# it there. Untracked as of the sync-widening change; regenerate with `npx grunt configTests`,
# which every CI job, the Dockerfile and the documented local setup already run.
src/core/config/modules/*
src/core/config/OperationConfig.json
src/core/operations/index.mjs
tests/operations/index.mjs
src/node/config/OperationConfig.json
src/node/index.mjs

# Also generated, by src/core/config/scripts/generateHTMLEntities.mjs -- a sixth path, added
# upstream in v11.4.0 and gitignored there too. Listed here BEFORE its generator reaches this
# fork (it arrives with the v11.4.0 sync) precisely so the 2,068-line artefact cannot be
# committed in the interim, which is exactly what happened once and had to be undone.
src/core/lib/HTMLEntities.mjs

# Secrets. Nothing matching this may ever be committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Logs
*.log

# Local toolchain pin. `.nvmrc` IS committed (it is the shared Node version); `.node-version`
# is left to individual setups.
.node-version

# Archives and image tarballs
*.tar.gz
*.tgz

# AI assistant local files
CLAUDE.local.md
GEMINI.md
WARP.md

# Coverage and test artifacts
coverage/
test-results/
.nyc_output/

# The default recipe store. `CYBERCHEF_RECIPE_STORAGE` defaults to ./recipes.json, so running the
# server or the examples from a checkout writes one into the repository root. It is user data --
# and it may hold keys and IVs, since a saved recipe carries its arguments.
recipes.json
recipes.json.backup
recipes.json.bak
recipes.json.*.tmp

# Reference checkouts for the external-project integration work (docs/planning/ext-proj-int/).
# `ref-proj/CyberChef` is a tracked submodule and stays visible -- see the note below; the other
# clones are local working copies of third-party repositories and are nobody else's business.
/ref-proj/*
!/ref-proj/CyberChef

# Antigravity PR reviewer: large-diff on-disk handoff (transient, removed by the script).
/.agy-review-work/

# NOT ignored, and deliberately so:
#
#   ref-proj/          A declared submodule in .gitmodules, tracked as a gitlink. Ignoring a
#                      tracked path is a contradiction -- it forced `git add -f` in both
#                      upstream-sync.yml and upstream-monitor.yml. The submodule's CONTENTS are
#                      managed by its own repository, not from here.
#
# Removed as stale:
#
#   travis.log         This project has never used Travis; CI is GitHub Actions.
#   tests/browser/*    The web app and its browser tests were removed in v1.7.1, and
#                      upstream-sync.yml fails the run if a sync tries to reintroduce them.
